  "id": "digital-divide",
  "term": "digital divide",
  "definition": "Digital divide is the gap in how people engage with digital technology, shaped by unequal resources such as knowledge, support, information, and money. It can involve differences in motivation to use technology, access to devices and internet infrastructure, digital skills, and the extent of technology use, and these gaps can restrict participation in everyday social life and reinforce existing inequalities.",
